from pathlib import Path
import re,html,difflib,markdown,json
O=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;R=O.parents[3]
def render(s):return markdown.markdown(re.sub(r'<!--\s*@[^>]*-->','',s),extensions=['extra','sane_lists'])
def image(n,c):return '<figure><a href="'+n+'.png"><img loading="lazy" src="'+n+'.png" alt="'+html.escape(c,quote=True)+'"></a><figcaption>'+c+'</figcaption></figure>'
before=(O/'Color_Paint.before.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8');after=(R/'commons/maps/Color_Paint/final.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
assert after==(O/'Color_Paint.after.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(O.parent/'2026-09-23-array-molnar-volume/index.html').read_text(encoding='utf-8'),re.S)[1]
page='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Paint — the surface keeps working</title><style>'+css+'</style></head><body><main>'
page+='''<div class="eyebrow">Ada Research · Colour · 23 September 2026</div><h1>The surface keeps working.</h1><p class="intro">You return the ball.<br>The painting has not finished.</p><p class="status">Applied to <strong>Color_Paint/final.md</strong>: one shared native illustration. Every existing paragraph and code excerpt is preserved.</p><nav><a href="#encounter">Two gestures</a><a href="#comparison">What changed</a><a href="#reading">Read the chapter</a><a href="#evidence">Evidence</a><a href="/compose/sources?map=Color_Paint&amp;doc=final">Read and comment</a></nav>'''
page+='<section id="encounter"><h2>A mark keeps changing after you leave it</h2>'+image('the-surface-keeps-working','Four successive views of the same working museum canvas. A supplied gesture joins the automatic line; releasing the pigment ends that input and returns the ball to the tray. The later image keeps changing. The automatic brush runs throughout.')+'<p>At the previous grid, a colour remained at its address until another write replaced it. Here the retained image itself is rewritten. That difference already carries the chapter’s question about authorship and memory.</p>'+image('at-the-tray','The actual tray and canvas, viewed from the position reached by the ordinary museum walker plus eye height. Thirty pigments remain available.')+'<details><summary>The existing Albers comparison</summary>'+image('albers-studies','Several of the existing Albers studies, seen through an opening. This is a partial view of the gallery; the runtime count confirms 98 studies remain. Their held arrangements provide the chapter’s comparison with the changing canvas.')+'</details></section>'
page+='<section id="comparison"><h2>Give the existing prose an image</h2><p>No prose needed cutting or replacing in this hall. The automatic gesture, your gesture, finite drawing positions, fading toward white, different clocks and the return from the Albers studies already make a connected investigation. The new figure appears immediately after “Which part of the image can you still call yours?”</p><div class="pair"><div><h3>Before</h3><p>Which part of the image can you still call yours?</p><p>The canvas has its own addresses…</p></div><div><h3>Now</h3><p>The same paragraphs, with four native states between them.</p>'+image('the-surface-keeps-working','A pigment ball is held and moved across the automatic line, then released. The ball returns to the tray while the painting continues to change.')+'</div></div><p><a href="Color_Paint.diff">Exact manuscript diff</a> · <a href="source-changes.diff">Companion evidence notes</a></p></section>'
page+='<section id="reading"><article class="reading">'+render(after)+'</article></section>'
page+='''<section id="evidence" class="evidence"><h2>What was checked</h2><p>30 focused assertions pass in the isolated production museum. The real pigment pickup, ray hit, rectangular UV mapping, release and return work. Automatic input continues during the supplied gesture and after release. The selected ball retains its live orange colour, 24-pixel brush radius and 64 snap divisions; it writes 79 samples. No brush settings were overridden.</p><p>Supplied key input drives the ordinary museum controller to the tray and back on the existing floor. The 98 Albers studies remain. No production scene, script, shader, map or primary selection changed.</p><details><summary>Does the surface change without another brush mark?</summary>'''
page+=image('feedback-diagnostic','A separate diagnostic pauses automatic input after the manual ball is released and its pending input has cleared. This is a probe condition, not a visitor control. Over 120 rendered frames, the retained image shifts and fades toward white.')
page+='''<p>Mean RGB distance from white falls from 0.21413 to 0.15950 while both inputs are quiet. GPU pixels change, and the brush queue is empty. This supports image feedback and fading; it is not evidence of physical pigment mixing. Automatic input is restored after the diagnostic.</p></details><p>The first gallery camera was mostly occluded; the retained closer view still shows only part of the wall through its opening. It is supplementary to the canvas figure. All four canvas views share a camera; the diagnostic is shown separately.</p><p>No tracked hand or headset, colour-calibration, learner or performance result is claimed. No live restart, live bake/save overwrite, commit or frozen book/audio rebuild.</p><p><a href="report.json">Runtime record</a> · <a href="source_manifest.json">Capture inputs</a> · <a href="verification.json">Preservation and publication checks</a> · <a href="SUMMARY.md">Findings and decisions</a></p></section><footer>Next: Color_Walls — colour helps organise the room itself.</footer></main></body></html>'''
(O/'index.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
diffs=[]
for rel in json.loads((O/'baseline-hashes.json').read_text()):
 if rel.endswith('/final.md'):continue
 diffs.extend(difflib.unified_diff((O/'before'/rel).read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines(True),(R/rel).read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines(True),fromfile='before/'+rel,tofile=rel))
(O/'source-changes.diff').write_text(''.join(diffs),encoding='utf-8')
print('Built current reading and exact changes.')
